## 4. Implemented backend

### Endpoints (live)

| Method | Path | Purpose |
|--------|------|---------|
| GET | `/health` | Health check (+ Kaggle reachability, `text_provider`, LLM status) |
| POST | `/upload_pdf` | Save PDF, extract pages; optional `?page_start=&page_end=`; returns `timing` (receive/extract/total seconds) |
| POST | `/build_topics` | Send extracted text to text provider (Kaggle Llama / Azure) → topic tree; returns `timing.total_seconds` |
| GET | `/topic/{topic_id}` | Topic metadata, source text, LLM explanation, images |
| POST | `/tts` | `{ text, voice? }` → MP3 audio |
| GET | `/debug/text` | Smoke-test text provider (Kaggle Llama or Azure chat) |
| GET | `/debug/azure` | Smoke-test TTS and image Azure deployments |
| GET | `/debug/extraction` | Per-page extraction summary |
| GET | `/debug/extraction/{page}` | Full page text; `?include_image_data=true` for base64 |
| GET | `/debug/topics` | Full built topic tree + `topics_by_id` |

### Endpoints (planned)

| Method | Path | Purpose |
|--------|------|---------|
| POST | `/ask` | `{ topic_id, question }` grounded answer |

### State (in-memory v1)

- `_active_extraction` — full per-page text + images; cleared on new upload
- `_active_topics` — topic tree + flat `topics_by_id`; cleared on new upload
- `_explanation_cache` in `topic_detail.py` — per-topic LLM explanations; cleared on new upload
- Resets on server restart (`# TODO v2`: disk cache)

### PDF extraction (`pdf_extract.py`)

- **PyMuPDF** (`fitz` / `pymupdf`): images via `get_images(full=True)` + `get_image_rects`; skip icons < 50px. `fitz` import shows deprecation warning — harmless for v1.
- **Text backends:** `CHAPTERWISE_TEXT_EXTRACTOR=pdfplumber` (default) or `rapidocr`. Laptop dev often uses **rapidocr** with `CHAPTERWISE_RAPIDOCR_FORCE=0` (digital pages use PyMuPDF `get_text`, not full OCR every page).
- **pdfplumber**: page text when extractor is pdfplumber; single open per page for text + overlap word counts
- **Parallel extraction:** `ProcessPoolExecutor` on Linux/Kaggle; `ThreadPoolExecutor` on Windows. `CHAPTERWISE_EXTRACT_WORKERS` (Kaggle default: CPU count).
- **Page-range extract:** `extract_document(pdf_path, page_start=, page_end=)` — only parses requested pages; returns `num_pages` (PDF total), `page_start`, `page_end`, `pages`.
- **Header/footer detection:** samples **36 evenly spaced pages** (not full PDF) via `PDFMetadataAnalyzer`; result **cached** by path + size + SHA256(head 64KB + tail 64KB). Fixes ~90s header scan on partial extracts (e.g. pages 1–10).
- **Debug timing:** `CHAPTERWISE_DEBUG_TIMING=1` logs per-phase seconds (pdf open, header/footer, rapidocr, images, worker pool).
- **Kaggle defaults** (in `chapterwise_gpu_server.py`): deferred image base64, skip overlap counts, process pool.
- `# TODO v2`: classify formula vs decorative images; defer base64 until topic open; skip re-upload if PDF hash unchanged on Kaggle

### Kaggle remote extraction (`kaggle_client.py`, `kaggle/chapterwise_gpu_server.py`)

- **Dataset:** `eakeswar/chapterwise-models` on Kaggle — publish via `backend/kaggle/publish_chapterwise_dataset.bat`
- **Flow:** laptop saves PDF → chunked upload to Kaggle → async extract → poll status → fetch result JSON
- **`kaggle_client.py`:** byte uploads via `_post_with_retry()`; JSON chat via `_post_json_with_retry()` → `POST /chat/completions`
- **`EXTRACT_PROVIDER`:** `local` | `kaggle` | `auto` (fallback to local if Kaggle fails). **`local` recommended for laptop dev** with page-range testing.
- **Tunnel:** cloudflared `trycloudflare.com` URL changes each notebook session → update `KAGGLE_API_BASE_URL` in `.env`
- **Large PDF fixes (2026-07-24):**
  - Chunked upload: `POST /upload_chunk` (4 MB parts, `KAGGLE_UPLOAD_CHUNK_BYTES`)
  - Async extract: `POST /extract` → poll `GET /extract/status` → `GET /extract/result` (avoids Cloudflare 524)
  - Poll retries: `KAGGLE_POLL_TIMEOUT=90`, `KAGGLE_UPLOAD_RETRIES=3`
- **Kaggle server endpoints:** `/health`, `/chat/completions`, `/upload_pdf`, `/upload_chunk`, `/extract`, `/extract/status`, `/extract/result`, `/upload_and_extract` (small files only)
- **Kaggle LLM (`llm_server.py`):** default `meta-llama/Llama-3.2-1B-Instruct` (4-bit on GPU). Requires `HF_TOKEN` on notebook + **gated-model access** on Hugging Face. Set `CHAPTERWISE_LLM_PRELOAD=1` to load at startup.
  - **Defaults (2026-08-10):** `CHAPTERWISE_LLM_MAX_INPUT_CHARS=12000`, `CHAPTERWISE_LLM_MAX_NEW_TOKENS=1024`, `CHAPTERWISE_LLM_ASSISTANT_CAP_CHARS=2000`.
  - **Truncation:** enforces total char budget across **all** messages (caps assistant, trims page chunk, not only last user). `torch.cuda.empty_cache()` after each generate.
  - **Generation:** `repetition_penalty=1.2`, `no_repeat_ngram_size=4`. `top_p` warning from transformers config is harmless.
  - **Notebook cell 2** should set the limits above (+ optional `PYTORCH_ALLOC_CONF=expandable_segments:True`) before starting the server.
- **Note:** PDF parsing uses **CPU** (PyMuPDF/pdfplumber); **GPU** used for Llama chat via `POST /chat/completions`.
- `# TODO v2`: host extract on Azure Container Apps + Blob instead of free Cloudflare tunnel

---

### Topic building (`topic_builder.py`)

- **`TEXT_PROVIDER`:** `kaggle` | `azure` | `auto` — routed via `text_provider.py` → Kaggle `/chat/completions` or Azure chat
- **Current default (laptop):** `TEXT_PROVIDER=kaggle` → **`meta-llama/Llama-3.2-1B-Instruct`** on Kaggle GPU
- Chunks by page range — default from **`CHAPTERWISE_TOPIC_CHUNK_PAGES`** (laptop dev: **8**). `/build_topics` uses env default via `DEFAULT_CHUNK_PAGES` (was hardcoded 18 in `main.py`).
- Strict JSON schema: `{ chapters: [{ title, page_start, page_end, sections: [...] }] }`
- Chunks concatenated in order; IDs assigned (`ch1`, `ch1_s1`, `ch1_s1_ss1`, …)
- `extract_topic_json()` + `_repair_topic_json_string()` repair malformed LLM JSON; `_call_topic_model()` retries once with “valid JSON only” follow-up (**assistant retry capped at 2000 chars** via `CHAPTERWISE_TOPIC_RETRY_CHARS`, was 12000)
- **Prompt rules (2026-08-10):** Activity boxes never become chapters/sections; hard limits (≤4 sections, ≤3 subsections per chunk); placeholder worked example + `_ANTI_LEAK_SENTENCE`; copy numbered headings from source; empty subsections when no real subheading/Activity.
- **Sanity warnings:** `_warn_chunk_tree_sanity()` — too many chapters, Activity in titles, prompt leakage, sibling near-duplicate titles.
- Optional body on `/build_topics`: `{ page_start, page_end, chunk_pages }` for testing a single chapter

---

## 5. Implemented frontend

- **UploadPanel:** PDF upload → `/upload_pdf` → `/build_topics`; optional “Test first pages only” passes `?page_start=1&page_end=N` to **upload** (partial extract) and build_topics; shows upload/extract + build timing after success
- **TopicTree:** Collapsible chapter → section → subsection; **never re-sort** client-side
- **TopicView:** Fetches `GET /topic/{id}`; shows **LLM explanation** + source text + image gallery; **Listen** calls `POST /tts` with title + explanation (falls back to source text); shimmer skeleton while loading
- **UploadLoadingScreen:** Animated main-panel loading during upload/build (shimmer progress bar + step labels + **live elapsed timer** + layout preview)
- **DocContext:** `topicTree`, `activeTopicId`, `topicCache`, `uploadTiming`, `buildTiming`, upload/build phases
- **App.jsx:** Sidebar + `TopicView` or `UploadLoadingScreen` in main panel
- Functional components, hooks only, **no `<form>` tags**, use `onClick` / file input handlers

### Run commands

```powershell
# Backend (port 8766)
python backend/main.py

# Frontend (port 5173)
cd frontend && npm run dev
```

```powershell
# Install deps (once)
python -m pip install --target backend/vendor -r backend/requirements.txt
cd frontend && npm install
```

