## 10. Coding preferences

- Python 3.11+, FastAPI, async where possible
- pip installs → `backend/vendor/` via `--target`
- Print logging OK for v1
- **Ask for approval before editing existing files** unless the user explicitly says to proceed/build/implement
- Never commit `backend/.env`, `backend/vendor/`, `backend/active_doc.pdf`
- Never hardcode API keys in source
- Keep changes scoped; match existing style
- Frontend: minimal CSS (no Tailwind in chapterwise v1), functional components only

---

## 11. Known issues & ops

- **Text/chat:** `TEXT_PROVIDER=kaggle` uses Kaggle `POST /chat/completions` (Llama on GPU). `auto` falls back to Azure if Kaggle text fails. Verify with `GET /debug/text` (`llm_loaded: true` on Kaggle health when preloaded).
- **Azure chat (optional):** Only required when `TEXT_PROVIDER=azure` or as auto fallback. TTS and images still use `services.ai.azure.com`. Verify TTS/images with `GET /debug/azure`. **`gpt-4o-mini` chat deployment still not provisioned** on `edzhub-resource`.
- **Azure endpoints:** Text chat → `AZURE_OPENAI_BASE_URL`; TTS + images → `AZURE_TTS_BASE_URL` / `AZURE_IMAGES_BASE_URL` (services endpoint, must include `/openai/v1`).
- **Kaggle tunnel:** Free `trycloudflare.com` URLs are ephemeral — refresh `KAGGLE_API_BASE_URL` each notebook run. **`/health` is fast**; **`/chat/completions` can fail with 502** when the tunnel loses Kaggle during a long LLM call (often on JSON **retry** after malformed first response). `KAGGLE_API_SECRET` must **exactly match** notebook cell 2. Prefer **`EXTRACT_PROVIDER=local`** for fast dev; use `auto` or `kaggle` for full offloaded extract.
- **Kaggle Llama gated model:** Accept license on https://huggingface.co/meta-llama/Llama-3.2-1B-Instruct (“Expand to review and access”); set `HF_TOKEN` in notebook. 403 “not in authorized list” → HF access not granted yet.
- **Kaggle Llama runtime:** Use `CHAPTERWISE_LLM_PRELOAD=1`. CUDA OOM on T4 → `CHAPTERWISE_TOPIC_CHUNK_PAGES=8`, `CHAPTERWISE_LLM_MAX_INPUT_CHARS=12000`, `CHAPTERWISE_LLM_MAX_NEW_TOKENS=1024`, republish dataset after `llm_server.py` changes. Llama 1B may return malformed topic JSON → repair + retry in `topic_builder.py` (retry assistant capped at 2000 chars).
- **Large PDFs (e.g. 300 MB):** Browser sends full file to laptop every upload. “Test first pages only” limits **extract** page range, not upload size. Kaggle path uploads all 76×4 MB chunks before extract. Local extract of 15–20 pages from 301 MB PDF ≈ 3–5 min on Windows.
- Only one upload/build at a time (`_extraction_lock`); backend blocks `/health` during active job
- **Port 8766 in use:** Stop prior `python backend/main.py` (Ctrl+C) before restarting
- Restart backend after `.env` changes; restart clears in-memory extraction/topics/explanations
- Frontend dev server: port **5173** — must be running separately (`npm run dev`)
- After Kaggle code changes: republish dataset + re-run notebook cells 1–2; copy new tunnel URL to `.env`
- Kaggle notebook pip warnings (`dopamine-rl`/`gym`, `gradio`/`pillow`) are harmless

---

## 12. Next step when user says “continue”

**Next:** (1) Kaggle: attach latest `chapterwise-models`, re-run cells 1–2, refresh tunnel URL. (2) End-to-end: upload (Test first pages only) → build topics → topic tree → open topic → explanation + Listen. (3) **Step 5:** `qa.py` + `/ask` + `AskPanel`. (4) Step 7 image routing incrementally. (5) `# TODO v2`: skip Kaggle upload when page range set; background extract; disk cache.

**Dev defaults (2026-08-10):** `EXTRACT_PROVIDER=local`, `TEXT_PROVIDER=kaggle`, `CHAPTERWISE_TOPIC_CHUNK_PAGES=8`, `CHAPTERWISE_TEXT_EXTRACTOR=rapidocr`. Kaggle notebook cell 2: `HF_TOKEN`, `CHAPTERWISE_LLM_PRELOAD=1`, `CHAPTERWISE_LLM_4BIT=1`, `CHAPTERWISE_LLM_MAX_INPUT_CHARS=12000`, `CHAPTERWISE_LLM_MAX_NEW_TOKENS=1024`.
